From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:35:31 -0300
Subject: drm/nouveau/dispnv50: declare CD=5 in the GCP at 10 bpc

At 10 bpc the GCP goes out with CD=0 (colour depth not indicated) on a
30-bpp link. HDMI 1.4b section 6.5.3 specifies CD=5 for 30 bpp, with the
packing phase of the four-pixel group. This adds the 10 bpc case with
the same phase rule the 12 bpc case uses.

Tested on this branch with an RTX 3060 (GA106) and two Sony 3D TVs,
KDL-46HX855 and KDL-46EX725 (over a 10 m cable): 12, 10 and 8 bpc and
3D at 12 bpc, including 1080p24 frame packing, all display. With and
without this change 10 bpc displays and the TVs report 10-bit, so on
these sinks it is for compliance with the specification and for sinks
that rely on CD, not a visible fix.

It comes from our withdrawn series:
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260923201930.1836730-1-Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com/

Assisted-by: Claude-Opus-5.5
Assisted-by: GPT-5.6-Sol
Assisted-by: Kimi-K3
Assisted-by: GLM-5.3
Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
(cherry picked from commit c4c27ea220184e51f2dc134ecccf4e6eafb4381b)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c       | 6 +++++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/include/nvif/if0012.h | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c
index c47b4d19e3a453a61d75ed3e89ea39e9e1085ca2..c45456eef645d26fba94eb37f9ea1123c8964cfc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/dispnv50/disp.c
@@ -1019,11 +1019,15 @@ nv50_hdmi_enable(struct drm_encoder *encoder, struct nouveau_crtc *nv_crtc,
 	tmds_clock = hw.crtc_clock * asyh->or.bpc / 8;
 
 	/* At 12 bpc, GCP SB1 carries CD=6 and a packing phase selected by the
-	 * parity of the back porch plus active width.
+	 * parity of the back porch plus active width. At 10 bpc it carries
+	 * CD=5 and the phase within the four-pixel group (HDMI 1.4b 6.5.3).
 	 */
 	if (asyh->or.bpc == 12)
 		gcp_sb1 = 0x06 | ((hw.crtc_htotal - hw.crtc_hsync_end +
 				   hw.crtc_hdisplay) & 1 ? 0x10 : 0x20);
+	else if (asyh->or.bpc == 10)
+		gcp_sb1 = 0x05 | (((hw.crtc_htotal - hw.crtc_hsync_end +
+				    hw.crtc_hdisplay) & 3) << 4);
 
 	max_ac_packet  = mode->htotal - mode->hdisplay;
 	max_ac_packet -= rekey;
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/include/nvif/if0012.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/include/nvif/if0012.h
index 022df916af49b68cdc279d591178e4f222b8fc47..9e0dafe3889399a2c7667c7a5b7154d2f3f10c58 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/include/nvif/if0012.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/include/nvif/if0012.h
@@ -176,7 +176,7 @@ union nvif_outp_hdmi_args {
 		__u8 scdc_scrambling;
 		__u8 scdc_low_rates;
 		__u32 khz;
-		/* GCP SB1: CD[3:0], PP[7:4], zero below 12 bpc. */
+		/* GCP SB1: CD[3:0], PP[7:4], zero below 10 bpc. */
 		__u8 gcp_sb1;
 		__u8 pad0d[3];
 	} v0;
